===Etymology===
Zorc (1985) surmises it to possibly be from {{bor|tl|es|domingo||Sunday}}, which was possibly mistakenly analyzed as {{m|tl|luminggo}} (e.g. ''Luminggo na'', "It's Sunday", which could have been taken to mean "It's been a week"), from which the word is derived by removing the seeming infix {{m|tl|-um-}} and early change from ⟨d⟩ to ⟨l⟩. However, according to Wolff (1976), it could also be from {{bor|tl|ms|minggu||week}}, which is from {{der|tl|pt|domingo||Sunday}}. Wolff argues that the change in initial nasal to ⟨l⟩ is also attested for {{w|Tagalog language|Tagalog}} {{m|tl|langka}} and {{w|Malay language|Malay}} {{m|ms|nangka}}.

